 "drivingQuestion": "Must the remaining hairsbreadth of corona surround all or most of the member?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "Rava Tosfa'a resolves Ravina's dilemma: a majority, toward the head.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "yevamot.75b.12",
   "daf": "75b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "וְאִם נִשְׁתַּיֵּיר מֵעֲטָרָה כּוּ׳. יָתֵיב רָבִינָא וְקָמִיבַּעְיָא לֵיהּ: מְלֹא הַחוּט שֶׁאָמְרוּ, עַל פְּנֵי כּוּלָּהּ אוֹ עַל פְּנֵי רוּבָּהּ? אֲמַר לֵיהּ רָבָא תּוֹסְפָאָה לְרָבִינָא: מְלֹא הַחוּט — עַל פְּנֵי רוּבָּהּ, וּכְלַפֵּי רֵישָׁא.",
   "en": "It is taught in the mishna that «if there remains» a portion «of the corona,» even as much as a hairsbreadth, he is still fit. «Ravina sat and raised the» following «dilemma:» This «hairsbreadth of which they spoke,» must it surround «the entire» member «or» only «a majority of it? Rava Tosfa’a said to Ravina: A hairsbreadth» of the corona must surround «a majority» of the member, «and toward its head,» that is, in the portion closer to the body."
  }
 ],
